Rule 1 (input array must have a floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must have floating-point dtype and non-negative dimension sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8) ∧ (if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must have non-negative rank and float-compatible dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) > 5 ∧ dtype_(v_1) < 9
>>
Rule 4 (input floating-point tensor with at least one dimension must have positive shapes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8)
>>
Rule 5 (input array dtype must not be bool, integer, complex, or non-numeric)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, 5] : dtype_(v_1) ≠ i) ∧ (∀j ∈ [9, 12] : dtype_(v_1) ≠ j)
>>
Rule 6 (2D tensor input must have positive dimensions and floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 7 (1D vector input must have positive length and floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 8 (scalar tensor input must be 0-dimensional with floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8)
>>
Rule 9 (4D tensor input must have positive shape dimensions and floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, 3] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 10 (3D tensor input must have positive dimensions along all three axes and floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0 ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 11 (non-empty array must have well-ordered min and max values and floating-point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1) ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
